From ac35fededb710b607f863844d8774cb6b57078d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:29:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 40/48] F17: the debug page opens the production model page (no
 backend)

The development phone has no MOSIP backend, so nobody can log in as a
supervisor and the home page's "Face liveness models" task is never
shown. The debug page (Login page, "Liveness test"; debug and profile
builds only) now has "Face liveness models (production page)". It
opens the same ModelBundlePage with the same production Pigeon methods
(the file picker, installZip, reload, REG-EVT-019).
- While that page is open, a diagnostics-only override stands in for
  the supervisor role: LivenessServiceHolder.setDiagnosticModelBundle
  Override (Pigeon setModelBundleDiagnosticOverride). It takes effect
  only when the holder was built with diagnostics
  (BuildConfig.LIVENESS_DIAGNOSTICS), so release builds ignore it; the
  native method also passes it on only in diagnostics builds. The
  config switch still applies. The debug page clears the override when
  the page closes.
- Every action that the override allowed is audited with
  roleCheck=diagnostics-override (AndroidAuditSink.modelBundle); a real
  supervisor's actions never carry it.

Tests: LivenessOfflineModelInstallTest 10 (3 new: release builds ignore
the override; a debug build's override allows install and rollback and
audits roleCheck=diagnostics-override, and closing the page or the
config switch turns it off; a tampered zip claiming an older version
is INVALID with MODEL_INTEGRITY_FAILED, the untouched files NOT_NEWER).
Module tests 105, Flutter liveness tests 90, all passing. The arm64
debug and release APKs build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
